# Lab 6 – Regression and Classification Models

## Objective

The objective of this lab was to understand the difference between regression and classification problems by building, training, and evaluating machine learning models for each type of task.

## What I Did

In this lab, I built a **Linear Regression** model to predict Titanic passenger fares using features such as age and passenger class. I evaluated the model using **Mean Squared Error (MSE)** and interpreted the model's coefficients to understand how each feature influenced the predictions.

I also created a **Logistic Regression** model to predict whether a Titanic passenger survived. After preparing the data and encoding categorical variables, I trained the model and evaluated its performance using **accuracy**. This provided hands-on experience with two of the most common supervised learning algorithms.

## What I Learned

This lab helped me understand the fundamental difference between regression and classification. I learned when each type of model should be used, how to train and evaluate them, and why different evaluation metrics are appropriate depending on whether the model predicts numerical values or categories.

